From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Bound the remaining long Bringup-Bench workloads
Purpose: Keeps expensive searches and simulations useful within RTL evaluation budgets.
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

The bounded inputs still exercise each workload's core algorithm. The
upstream submodule and reference hashes remain unchanged.

diff --git a/ackermann/ackermann.c b/ackermann/ackermann.c
--- a/ackermann/ackermann.c
+++ b/ackermann/ackermann.c
@@ -1,1 +1,3 @@
+/* Evaluates a bounded grid of memoized Ackermann calls. */
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 */
 /* Ackermann.c: calculate the Ackermann function (as far as that is possible),
@@ -108,7 +110,7 @@
 #include "libmin.h"
 
-#define AMAX 5  /* largest arguments to contemplate. This is waaaaaaaaaay more than sufficient! */
+#define AMAX 4  /* Keep the recursive evaluation bounded for RTL simulation. */
 
 /* Play around with these definitions. Can you get a(1,4)? */
-#define MAX_X 0xFFFF  /* rows in storage array */
+#define MAX_X 64  /* AMAX=4 reaches x<=12; leave headroom without a 4 MiB BSS. */
 #define MAX_Y 0x10    /* columns in storage array */
